<feed xmlns="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom"><title>World | Deutsche Welle</title><subtitle type="html">World | Deutsche Welle</subtitle><id>https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><author><name>rssync</name></author><link rel="self" href="rss-en-world" type="application/atom+xml" /><link rel="alternate" href="https://www.dw.com/english/?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><link rel="via" href="https://rss.dw.com/xml/rss-en-world" type="application/rss+xml" /><entry><title>Gen Z protests: Do Baby Boomers really have it better than young people?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:460c323409a09a9f4c4db3403d85cf304790a702e830831110c44224ab0f5765</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:45:53Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T06:09:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854--e581c42657a0.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/gen-z-protests-do-baby-boomers-really-have-it-better-than-young-people/a-79918854?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Should young people in Germany be more worried about their future than Baby Boomers were in the 1980s and 1990s? Or should both generations take to the streets and protest together? DW checked the data.</summary><category term="Germany" /></entry><entry><title>SpaceX launches Starship rocket, fails to recover booster</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:c073b3b5f8460ee7a7b8c9105a47831f8ba0ea664482508f79f72a62b7fb874a</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:02Z</updated><published>2026-11-14T02:24:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/spacex-launches-starship-rocket-fails-to-recover-booster/a-79946091--bd09d60b45a7.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/spacex-launches-starship-rocket-fails-to-recover-booster/a-79946091?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">SpaceX had planned to catch and later reuse both stages of its biggest rocket for the first time. But the booster exploded over the Gulf of Mexico, while the spacecraft continued into orbit.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Tanker collides with cruise ship on Mississippi in New Orleans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0a8378890ce2461292cb5fd29d0f74303ecac23c697433352254e7db579eeb1b</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:08Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T21:31:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/tanker-collides-with-cruise-ship-on-mississippi-in-new-orleans/a-79945080--29dd618b519d.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/tanker-collides-with-cruise-ship-on-mississippi-in-new-orleans/a-79945080?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A freighter collided with a cruise ship carrying around 130 people in New Orleans, causing the paddlewheel vessel to capsize. More than 30 people were hospitalized, but all passengers survived and were accounted for.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>The dangers of revising Europe's security architecture</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:b3fb681feee694d0849cf05d4bf7f4c38557840a982942fd856d7465575f7045</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:20Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T17:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049--ae25152ee718.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/the-dangers-of-revising-europe-s-security-architecture/a-79943049?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Experts warn against revising Europe's security framework because they say it would mean granting Moscow its longstanding wish of renegotiating postwar security on the continent.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Why does El Salvador's Bukele have troops in Haiti?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:a21acfb01cae27bce620a94a43107de38f46421a9f64459d51b3d2c58d13aad0</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:37:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/why-does-el-salvador-s-bukele-have-troops-in-haiti/a-79940771--dfce4a53e7c3.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/why-does-el-salvador-s-bukele-have-troops-in-haiti/a-79940771?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Haiti's Prime Minister congratulating El Salvador's President for a gang crackdown in Haiti has shone a light on the relationship between the two countries. What's going on, and where does the US stand?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Iran targeted US radar system in Bahrain</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:0ab6ac15af2eed1afddeee750ed3c28152264ae35a3553ce9de0c6a3ed593f6d</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:32:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/iran-targeted-us-radar-system-in-bahrain/a-79942640--6a6890129eef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/iran-targeted-us-radar-system-in-bahrain/a-79942640?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Iran claimed it struck US radar systems in Bahrain, while the US said it had intercepted the attacks. Clashes continue in the Strait of Hormuz, as the war remains in a state of de-escalation.</summary><category term="News" /></entry><entry><title>Beijing faces its Russia dilemma amid talk of Xi-Trump-Putin summit</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:71657691e686983ed2f23017b33457ea9a1637013dfd2ffd3ca3299477fb7dff</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T15:28:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-its-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427--4d68b234d525.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/beijing-faces-its-russia-dilemma-amid-talk-of-xi-trump-putin-summit/a-79942427?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">China is forced to tread carefully as it considers hosting a meeting between Xi Jinping, Vladimir Putin, and Donald Trump. While the optics are sure to favor Moscow, Beijing is risking its image at the global stage.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Indonesia's wiretapping scandal opens a political fault line</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:e3030e4ab34210e1bf578c088e763e5057e7c9238155df24be737a0fefca4250</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T14:29:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753--0451bf449bfd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/indonesia-s-wiretapping-scandal-opens-a-political-fault-line/a-79939753?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">Senior police officers are accused of illegally monitoring President Prabowo Subianto, exposing rival networks within Indonesia's security establishment and renewing concerns about political misuse of surveillance.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Is the AI bubble bursting just as Anthropic goes public?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:953002283f1a057bcdaf65f5475b1865d11da2ab95d436bac3cc592186de2106</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T12:27:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537--10f78cdc2264.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/is-the-ai-bubble-bursting-just-as-anthropic-goes-public/a-79896537?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">The sharp sell-off in tech stocks after the US midterms has cast doubt on Anthropic's looming IPO. Yet with hundreds of billions still being invested, some think the AI party is still in full swing.</summary><category term="Business" /></entry><entry><title>Humanitarian situation in Gaza worsens amid political deadlock</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:880829bba07e0335d99f8865fb3520f8ef82c13b72fe09df795a0b1ea391e664</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T09:30:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/humanitarian-situation-in-gaza-worsens-amid-political-deadlock/a-79931403--a8a6020c54fc.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/humanitarian-situation-in-gaza-worsens-amid-political-deadlock/a-79931403?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">In war-battered Gaza, heavy rain flooded and damaged thousands of tents. Several people died. Could pressure by Trump's Board of Peace on Israel and Hamas help to ease the humanitarian crisis amid stalled peace talks?</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>Czechia braces for massive protest against public media reform plans</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:ef9d5f421882277ca38e29f02d16bbba066f74c3143324ca0fd2ae4a1c1431a8</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:46:29Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:35:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533--a08ee7cdb27e.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/czechia-braces-for-massive-protest-against-public-media-reform-plans/a-79933533?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A fast-tracked bill to cut public media funding has sparked strikes, rallies and fears for the independence of public broadcasting in Czechia. A massive protest is planned for Prague on Sunday.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>After suffering its worst election result, what's next for the ANC — and for South Africa?</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:5dfe751e7082114bfb7c0cd80789271a99eb60c8c14e43f7784927e5865a6fb3</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-13T08:33:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/after-suffering-its-worst-election-result-what-s-next-for-the-anc-and-for-south-africa/a-79929902--0f5fc83270ef.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/after-suffering-its-worst-election-result-what-s-next-for-the-anc-and-for-south-africa/a-79929902?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A crushing local election result across the country has left South Africa's ruling ANC searching for answers. Experts say the vote reflects public frustration with service delivery failures — signaling a political shift.</summary><category term="World" /></entry><entry><title>EU leaders tussle over whom to send to Ukraine, Russia peace talks</title><id>urn:rssync:entry:3b3aa54d71b269905f23be78727de36deeea978cdd2b1a70bddfd301aba8554e</id><updated>2026-11-14T06:44:58Z</updated><published>2026-11-12T22:00:00Z</published><link rel="alternate" href="../../../pages/www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468--127d08162dcd.html" type="text/html" /><link rel="via" href="https://www.dw.com/en/eu-leaders-tussle-over-whom-to-send-to-ukraine-russia-peace-talks/a-79935468?maca=en-rss-en-world-4025-xml-mrss" /><summary type="html">A seat at the table for Europe now appears likely following comments by a US envoy who just held talks with Putin. But who will take that seat remains unclear.</summary><category term="World" /></entry></feed>
